    <tok fileIndex="0" linenr="2265" column="1" str="/**x * @brief Iterates through a BC command list, extracts any data a does maintenance operationsx *x * @param [in] iop_dev iop 1553 support structx * @param [out] arg pointer to iop wrapperx *x * @return status of the operation:x *  x- AIR_SUCCESSFUL: Data was sucessfully read.x * xx- AIR_TIMED_OUT: End of list.x *x * This function will obtain the list that is currently being processed byx * the bc core and will process the already completed commands. Each command isx * checked for errors and available data. Depending on the command type, some x * commands will be updated, others will have their data extracted. The function x * returns when there is data available to be read or when the command list as x * reached its end. The function starts processing the list in a previously read x * position. It then follows the branching structure of the list. x */"/>
